"""The objects of an ONI window, as ONI itself writes them.

Captured from a real project (Достоево, ONI Visual Studio 3.0) and parameterised: geometry, caption, address,
the window a key opens. Everything else — the defaults ONI puts into every object — is kept verbatim: a window
ONI opens without complaint is the whole point, and those defaults are not guessable.

`{raw}` — the address block (empty for a key that reads nothing), `{actions}` — what the key does,
`{window}` — the window it opens.
"""

